{"name":"Ms. Pac-Man Kiss","hex":"#ff00aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ms.","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Abbreviation of manuscript."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of m. (“month”)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ms."},{"term":"pac","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Pacoh."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of pack.","A moccasin with a sole made of leather or deerskin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pac"},{"term":"man","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Mandingo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male human.","All human males collectively: mankind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/man"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ms. Pac-Man","blocks":[{"text":"Ms. Pac-Man is a 1982 maze video game developed by General Computer Corporation (GCC) and published by Midway Manufacturing for arcades. It is a sequel to Pac-Man (1980), and the first entry in the series to not be made by Namco. Controlling the title character, Pac-Man's wife, the player is tasked with eating all of the pellets in an enclosed maze while avoiding four colored ghosts. Eating the larger \"power pellets\" lets the player eat the ghosts, which turn blue and flee."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/42/Ms._Pac-Man_flyer.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ms._Pac-Man","wikidata":"Q2141683"},{"title":"Ms.","blocks":[{"text":"Ms. or Ms is an English-language honorific used with the last name or full name of a woman, intended as a default form of address for women regardless of marital status. Like Miss and Mrs., the term Ms. has its origins in the female English title once used for all women, Mistress, the feminine form of Mister and Master. It originated in the 17th century and was revived into mainstream usage in the 20th century."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ms.","wikidata":"Q1951543"},{"title":"Pac-Man","blocks":[{"text":"Pac-Man, originally titled Puck Man in Japan, is a 1980 maze video game developed and published by Namco for arcades. It was released in Japan on May 22, 1980 and by Midway Manufacturing in North America in October 1980. The player controls Pac-Man, who must eat all the dots inside an enclosed maze while avoiding four colored ghosts. Eating large flashing dots called \"Power Pellets\" causes the ghosts to temporarily turn blue and vulnerable, allowing Pac-Man to eat the ghosts for bonus points."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/16/Pac_flyer.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pac-Man","wikidata":"Q173626"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss","wikidata":"Q7307"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Mspacman.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Mspacman.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Start of the game","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMspacman.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Gloria_Steinam_Endorsement_%283838080804%29.jpg/500px-Gloria_Steinam_Endorsement_%283838080804%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Gloria_Steinam_Endorsement_%283838080804%29.jpg/500px-Gloria_Steinam_Endorsement_%283838080804%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gloria Steinem, who founded the magazine Ms., popularising the term.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGloria_Steinam_Endorsement_(3838080804).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Geraldine_Ferraro%2C_first_female_Vice_Presidential_candidate_running_with_Presidential_candidate_Walter_Mondale%2C_visits_University_of_Texas_at_Arlington_campus_%2810006337%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Geraldine_Ferraro%2C_first_female_Vice_Presidential_candidate_running_with_Presidential_candidate_Walter_Mondale%2C_visits_University_of_Texas_at_Arlington_campus_%2810006337%29.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Geraldine_Ferraro%2C_first_female_Vice_Presidential_candidate_running_with_Presidential_candidate_Walter_Mondale%2C_visits_University_of_Texas_at_Arlington_campus_%2810006337%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Geraldine Ferraro, whose case encouraged the recognition of \"Ms.\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File